### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
# Replace this token with the one you get from login/register
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### --- AUTHENTICATION ---

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test Student",
    "email": "student@university.edu",
    "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login with user
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "student@university.edu",
    "password": "password123"
}

### --- RESOURCES ---

### 3. Get all resources (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/resources

### 4. Create a new resource (Protected)
# --> Make sure you replace @token at the top with your login token!
POST {{baseUrl}}/resources
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "Calculus 101 Midterm Notes",
    "subject": "Math",
    "topic": "Calculus",
    "fileUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/image/upload/sample.pdf",
    "tags": ["math", "midterm", "notes"]
}

### 5. Get a single resource by ID (Replace ID with one from Get All Resources response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/resources/YOUR_RESOURCE_ID_HERE

### 6. Generate Cloudinary Signature (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/resources/generate-signature
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- GAMIFICATION / VOTING ---

### 7. Upvote a resource (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/votes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "resourceId": "YOUR_RESOURCE_ID_HERE",
    "type": "up"
}

### 8. Downvote a resource (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/votes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "resourceId": "YOUR_RESOURCE_ID_HERE",
    "type": "down"
}
